ADY\",\"expected_rework_locality\":\"HIGH\",\"governing_intent\":\"Add a `--dry-run` flag to `tool export <dir>` that prints to stdout, one per line, the absolute paths a real export would write, in the existing export order, exits 0, and writes nothing. Behaviour without the flag must stay byte-identical.\",\"implementation_unknowns\":[\"Where the export CLI's argument parsing lives. The task states it is in `src/tool/export.py`, but if option registration sits in a separate CLI entry module, the stated scope may need a minimal touch there.\",\"How the export loop currently derives each output path. Dry-run must reuse the same path computation so the paths and order exactly match a real run.\",\"Whether a real run creates `<dir>` (or intermediate directories) when missing. If so, dry-run must skip that creation and still compute absolute paths for a directory that may not exist.\",\"How to make paths absolute (for example `os.path.abspath` versus `Path.resolve`), and whether a real run's paths involve symlink resolution. The chosen form must match 'exactly the paths a real run writes'.\",\"Whether export currently prints anything else to stdout (progress, summaries) that would contaminate dry-run output. The contract implies stdout should contain only the paths.\",\"The existing test framework and fixtures to use for asserting no filesystem changes, such as a tmp directory snapshot before and after.\"],\"independent_decision_centers\":[],\"material_risks\":[\"Path-equivalence drift: if dry-run computes paths through a separate code path, it may diverge from real-run paths in ordering, normalization or absolute-versus-relative form, violating 'exactly the paths a real run writes'.\",\"Hidden side effects: directory creation, temp files, caches or logs written during export setup could violate the no-write guarantee if they occur before the dry-run branch.\",\"Scope pressure: if CLI option wiring lives outside `src/tool/export.py`, strictly honouring the stated file 