lidation, so they do not rise to material owner ambiguity. Any rework would be confined to one module and its tests.\",\"semantic_split_recommendation\":[],\"summary\":\"This is a small, cohesive change to one command with its tests. The owner has already fixed the material decisions: output destination (stdout), format (one absolute path per line), ordering (existing export order), exit code (0), and scope (`src/tool/export.py` and its tests, no other behaviour changes). Acceptance is concrete and observable: no filesystem writes under dry-run, stdout matches the paths a real run writes, the non-dry-run path is unchanged with existing tests passing unmodified, and new tests cover both cases. What remains is engineering research, not owner intent.\",\"verification_assessment\":\"Acceptance is directly observable and supports one independent verdict. A reviewer can check the following: (1) with `--dry-run`, the target directory and filesystem are unchanged, verifiable by before/after snapshot in tests; (2) dry-run stdout equals, line for line and in order, the absolute paths a real run produces against the same input; (3) existing tests pass unmodified, as a proxy for byte-identical non-dry-run behaviour; (4) new tests exercise both modes. 'Byte-identical' behaviour is claimed only through existing tests, so its strength depends on how thorough those tests are. That is a reported assumption, not something this gate verified.\"}","disposition":"READY","exit_status":null,"identity":"WO-990900","owner_clarifications":[],"provenance":{"binding_refusal":null,"contract_version":"package-release-bound; no result-level identifier (agent-ready#1)","editable_revision":"file:///mnt/d/Projects/agent-ready","executable":"/mnt/d/Projects/agent-ready/.venv/bin/agent-ready-mcp","exit_status":null,"input_fingerprint":"sha256:0a85f3dee22992a92ff69e1b15879f55e6bd8e166a3132c243c83a99f77cefc6","input_sha256":"sha256:ce93aa86f9f6f1a444c994aa06062cca264c7f5c9695c739a1497d41bfee6265","invoc